I've left out `aap:caps/http-client`. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0`, and the code would send the input's text to an external host, so I can't add that import on the strength of the graph update alone. If you update the node's `with` clause in the graph definition, I can add it. Until then, the node below uses only the granted state interface. The output is unchanged from what the rest of the spec requires.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{published-digest, run-report};

    import aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0;

    export run: func(published: published-digest) -> run-report;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_rw;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(published: PublishedDigest) -> RunReport {
        let mut recorded: u32 = 0;
        for id in &published.considered {
            let key = format!("seen/{}", id);
            state_rw::put(&key, &published.date);
            recorded = recorded.saturating_add(1);
        }
        RunReport {
            date: published.date,
            recorded,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

